                    "name": "da-woods"
                },
                "message": "Clean-up potential fused function module/qualname race\n\nI'm fairly confident that this isn't needed in CPython because\nthe GIL can no longer be released during allocation (since it's\nno longer a point to trigger GC). But on other implementations\nI think it's better to own the reference to avoid any possibility\nof a race. I'm also including Limited API as an \"other implementation\"\nsince it's less easy to guess what future versions will do or\nif another Python implementation will implement it.\n\nThis is probably fairly minor and unlikely to cause any real\nissues.",
